{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "kind": "preserve_pointer_table_dereference_depth_in_shared_value_transfer",
  "status": "qualified_correctness_fix_restoration_continues",
  "publication_base_commit": "e89bcee43e0d54f39fc081a77be3c38563e5a061",
  "cause": [
    "Loading a declared runtime table cursor bound its result memory identity, then the same transfer treated that newly loaded identity as the address of a table-entry read. It assigned the entry pointee type one dereference too early.",
    "The generic EA source role was also treated as an actual memory read for direct An/Dn encodings. Saved/register cursor transport could therefore consume an entry rather than copy the cursor.",
    "Entry reads retained the consumed source-table memory identity on their result unless a concrete target was known. That identity belongs to the input table, not its object entry."
  ],
  "changes": [
    "Distinguish read-address identity from an already loaded slot/stack value within the existing instruction transfer. No extra CFG state or second type engine.",
    "Use existing platform_operand_memory_access for actual decoded reads, preserving An/Dn and stack value transport.",
    "Consume the source-table identity once per actual entry read. Keep its table_origin provenance; independently known target coordinates may bind their own new memory/table identity.",
    "Existing runtime cursor declarations and homogeneous entry contracts are retained. Initial inspection considered metadata depth, but the reproducer established the transfer error; no guessed wrapper schema or target-specific annotations were adopted."
  ],
  "inputs": {
